## Answer

The change targets **`pkg/cmd/gist/create/create.go`**, function **`createRun`** (lines 104–175).

Currently, the message-building logic is:

```go
processMessage := "Creating gist..."
completionMessage := "Created gist"
if gistName != "" {
    if len(files) > 1 {
        processMessage = "Creating gist with multiple files"
    } else {
        processMessage = fmt.Sprintf("Creating gist %s", gistName)
    }
    if opts.Public {
        completionMessage = fmt.Sprintf("Created %s gist %s", cs.Red("public"), gistName)
    } else {
        completionMessage = fmt.Sprintf("Created %s gist %s", cs.Green("secret"), gistName)
    }
}
```

The privacy status (`public`/`secret`, colored via `cs.Red`/`cs.Green`) is only inserted into `completionMessage` when `gistName != ""` — i.e., only when a real filename could be guessed via `guessGistName`. When creating a gist purely from stdin with no `--filename` override (so `guessGistName` returns `""`), the completion message falls back to the plain `"Created gist"`, omitting the privacy status entirely, per `Test_createRun`'s `"stdin arg"` case in `pkg/cmd/gist/create/create_test.go:271-291` (`wantStderr: "- Creating gist...\n✓ Created gist\n"`), matching issue #7644.

The fix modifies `createRun` to separate the "does a gist name exist" logic (which controls `processMessage`, i.e. whether to mention a filename) from the public/secret determination for `completionMessage`, so the privacy status (`Created public gist ...` / `Created secret gist ...`, or `Created public/secret gist` when there's no filename) is always included regardless of whether `gistName` is empty.

This also means the corresponding test file **`pkg/cmd/gist/create/create_test.go`** needs its `"stdin arg"` test case's `wantStderr` updated (line 278) to expect a privacy status (e.g. `"- Creating gist...\n✓ Created secret gist\n"`) instead of the current `"- Creating gist...\n✓ Created gist\n"`.

No other files reference this message-construction logic — `guessGistName`, `processFiles`, `createGist`, and `detectEmptyFiles` in the same file are unrelated helpers that remain unchanged.
